# Third-party code, and content that is not distributed

ColourWars is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). This file records what in the working
tree is not ColourWars' to license, and what is deliberately absent.

The engine is not covered here. It is a submodule at `external/labrador` with
its own LICENSE and its own NOTICE, and the third-party code it carries —
Microsoft's `DeviceResources` and `StepTimer`, Christer Ericson's collision
routines — is recorded there.

## Code carried in this repository

### rapidjson (MIT)

`external/rapidjson/` is vendored, with its own `license.txt` and `README.md`
beside it. Copyright (c) 2015 THL A29 Limited, a Tencent company, and Milo Yip.

This is a second copy — the engine vendors one too. That is deliberate rather
than an oversight of the split: the engine's is PRIVATE and no engine header
names the parser, so a client that parses files of its own asks for rapidjson
on its own account. This one is asked for on account of the save file and the
level files.

### Microsoft content tools (MIT)

Three build tools ship in `game/content/`, alongside the assets they produce:

- `game/content/sounds/sound_bank_1/XWBTool.exe` — the wave-bank compiler.
- `game/content/fonts/MakeSpriteFont.exe` — the sprite-font compiler.
- `game/content/textures/texconv.exe` — the texture converter.

Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. Licensed under the MIT License.
Source: https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTK and
https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTex

## Content that is deliberately not distributed

### Audio

`game/content/sounds/` ships the bank's definition (`sound_bank_1.json`), the
build tool, and the CMake recipe that turns source waves into
`sound_bank_1.xwb`. It does not ship the waves or the built bank.

Two reasons, and either alone would be enough:

1. **Licence.** Four of the twenty-four waves are commercial music tracks. They
   are not ColourWars' to redistribute under MIT or any other licence.
2. **Size.** The sources are 148 MB and the built bank is 154 MB, past
   GitHub's per-file limit.

A clone therefore has no wave bank, and this is handled rather than broken: the
manifest marks the bank optional, the loader substitutes a silent one, prints a
line saying so, and the game runs. See README, "Audio".

### Fonts

`game/content/fonts/` holds compiled `.spritefont` files built from system
fonts (Gill Sans MT, Courier New) with Microsoft's `MakeSpriteFont`. The
compiled glyph atlases are redistributed here on the same footing as any other
game asset built from a licensed system font; the fonts themselves are not
included and are not ColourWars' to license.
